      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is a \"we sort of noticed things work better if you do it this way\" kind of thing.\n\nIt is not a \"rule\".\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is a \"we sort of noticed things work better if you do it this way\" kind of thing.\n\nIt is not a \"rule\".\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "o9OUS5uoEdhMcYrP9qWVj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 312,
      "y": 351,
      "width": 629.1796875,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 820338871,
      "version": 612,
      "versionNonce": 330676889,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787767226395,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "@Component - to define a few different kinds of components\n\n- Pages\n    - These are components that are the target of a route.\n    - They have a selector, but it is never used*\n    - That means, don't use the selector of a page.\n- Container (a.k.a. \"Smart\")\n\n- Presentational (a.k.a \"Dumb\")\n    - give it some data, and it will do something with it.\n    - it might have outputs to let you know something happened.\n        - does not usually inject services, etc.\n\n\nPresentational are *usually* the ones you want to share.\nBut that's a refactoring.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "@Component - to define a few different kinds of components\n\n- Pages\n    - These are components that are the target of a route.\n    - They have a selector, but it is never used*\n    - That means, don't use the selector of a page.\n- Container (a.k.a. \"Smart\")\n\n- Presentational (a.k.a \"Dumb\")\n    - give it some data, and it will do something with it.\n    - it might have outputs to let you know something happened.\n        - does not usually inject services, etc.\n\n\nPresentational are *usually* the ones you want to share.\nBut that's a refactoring.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
